"tunnel.instructions" = "If it did not turn on: System Settings → General → Login Items & Extensions → Network Extensions (ⓘ) → turn on PrivacyBrowser → Done. On macOS 14: System Settings → Privacy & Security → Allow. Then allow adding the VPN configuration. The app must be in /Applications.";
"tunnel.intro" = "PrivacyBrowser's network extension sends the WebRTC of profiles with a SOCKS5 proxy through that proxy: pages get a relay (TURN) on a virtual address, which sends their UDP through the proxy's UDP ASSOCIATE. Sites and peers see the proxy's address, not this Mac's. The extension leaves the rest of the Mac's traffic alone.";
"tunnel.limits" = "Only the WebRTC of profiles with a SOCKS5 proxy without TLS goes through the extension (an HTTP proxy cannot carry UDP); the proxy must support UDP ASSOCIATE. Pages get relay candidates only. While the tunnel is connected macOS shows a VPN, and it runs one such VPN at a time: starting this tunnel disconnects another VPN app's tunnel (WireGuard, Tailscale, …), and when that one starts, this one stops — WebRTC in proxied profiles then fails, it does not fall back to this Mac's address.";
"tunnel.notBuilt.note" = "This build has no network extension. It needs a signed build (NE=1 scripts/build-app.sh): a paid Apple Developer account, the packet-tunnel entitlement for the app and the extension, and the app in /Applications.";
